.TH KEYPOP 1 "August 2026" "keypop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keypop \- elegant keystroke and mouse click visualizer for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keypop
[\fB\-b\fR \fIcolor\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIcolor\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIsize\fR]
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgeometry\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIopacity\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fItimeout\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keypop
is a lightweight, high-performance on-screen keystroke and mouse click visualization overlay written in C++20 for Wayland compositors. It captures input events via libinput and displays typed combinations, modifier keys, repeat counters, and mouse clicks in real time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " color"
Set background color as hexadecimal string (e.g. \fI#000000\fR or \fI000000\fR).
.TP
.BI \-c " color"
Set text foreground color as hexadecimal string (e.g. \fI#FFFFFF\fR).
.TP
.BI \-s " size"
Set font size in points (default: \fI65\fR).
.TP
.BI \-g " WxH"
Set window dimensions in pixels (default: \fI840x130\fR).
.TP
.BI \-o " opacity"
Set background opacity between 0.0 (transparent) and 1.0 (opaque) (default: \fI0.6\fR).
.TP
.BI \-t " ms"
Set auto-hide timeout in milliseconds. If set to \fI0\fR, the overlay will never hide automatically (default: \fI2000\fR).
.TP
.B \-v
Show version information and build metadata.
.TP
.B \-h
Show help usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/keypop/keypop.conf
User configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keypop.conf (5)
